  "id": "COMPOUND:42636 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Camelliquercetiside B appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways, all leading to the target NCI-H446. The first pathway involves Camelliquercetiside B directly targeting MIP, which is then a target of Sophoradiol, ultimately resulting in NCI-H446. The second pathway involves Camelliquercetiside B interacting with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is subsequently targeted by 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, again leading to NCI-H446. The third pathway involves Camelliquercetiside B targeting a complex lipid molecule, which in turn targets NCI-H446. These diverse mechanisms suggest that Camelliquercetiside B may act through different molecular pathways to influence NCI-H446, potentially through distinct cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with each step contributing to the overall effect on NCI-H446. The evidence supports the notion that Camelliquercetiside B may have a role in modulating NCI-H446 through multiple, possibly overlapping, mechanisms.",
